[38;5;189m[1;38;5;146m  1[m   [38;5;185m# lensd specification[m[m                                                                         
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m  2[m   [m                                                                                              
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m  3[m   What lensd guarantees, as definitions ([38;5;146m`**Def $Name (title).**`[m) and invariants[m               
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m  4[m   ([38;5;146m`**$Name (title).**`[m). Normative statements use[m                                              
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m  5[m   MUST. Every invariant names what checks it: a TLA+ model in spec/tla/ (each with a [m           
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m   [m   deliberately broken[m                                                                           
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m  6[m   "mutant" that TLC must reject), a Go test, or a runtime check. Go tests cite what they check [m 
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m   [m   with a[m                                                                                        
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m  7[m   comment directly above the test:[m                                                              
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m  8[m   [m                                                                                              
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m  9[m       [38;5;146m// Spec: $Frame.Timing §1 "quoted text from this file"[m[m                                    
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 10[m   [m                                                                                              
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 11[m   and code may cite the invariant it enforces ([38;5;146m`// $Sdk.NvrAgrees: ...`[m). A spec change and the [m
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m   [m   matching test[m                                                                                 
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 12[m   or model change go in the same commit. Values marked (code: …) also exist as constants; [m      
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m   [m   changing one[m                                                                                  
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 13[m   means changing the other. Liveness is stated as bounded-time rules on lensd's own clock [m      
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m   [m   ([38;5;212m$Time.Elapsed[m),[m                                                                              
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 14[m   not as TLA+ liveness properties. Trace verification (checking runtime traces against the [m     
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m   [m   models) is out[m                                                                                
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 15[m   of scope.[m                                                                                     
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 16[m   [m                                                                                              
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 17[m   [38;5;185m## Context (for readers without the code)[m[m                                                     
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 18[m   [m                                                                                              
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 19[m   lensd is a Go web gateway for two NVRs at one site. It relays live RTSP from the NVR (one[m     
[38;5;189m[38;5;102m 20[m   session per camera shared by all viewers), plays recordings through a vendor SDK helper [m      
